think Read line_slice.rye and line_pierce.rye to learn the idiom: exact integers, doubled coordinates, separating-axis crossing, compose-not-braid, insertion sort by an along-line key. line_slice orders pierced objects by line_order.project_label -- the CENTER projection.
think The crux for line_raycast: a physical drag enters the box whose NEAR FACE it reaches first (the slab-method entry parameter), which can differ from center order. Designed line_raycast reading the pierced set ordered by t_enter = max(t_x_lo, t_y_lo), each axis entry a rational (near_face - a)/d, held (num, den) den>0, compared by i128 cross-multiply. No float, no sqrt, no divide.
obs First scene tried (disjoint singletons) failed: proved a theorem on the way. line_order/line_slice project the CLUSTER center, not each object's box -- and objects whose bounding boxes overlap merge into one cluster. For a horizontal stroke, two objects both crossed with overlapping x-ranges necessarily share a bounding box (both y-ranges contain the stroke) -> same cluster. So genuine near-face-vs-center divergence happens exactly where line_slice already ties the objects on their shared cluster center and falls back to label order. That is the sharper, more honest crux.
obs Redesigned: a wide L shape P (box x[5,20]) swallowing a narrow block Q (box x[12,15]) into one cluster, pixels disjoint. Horizontal stroke A->B casts [A,P,Q,B] by near x-face; line_slice ties P,Q on the cluster center and orders by label -> [A,Q,P,B]. P and Q swap at ranks 1,2 -- the divergence on metal.
obs Deeper fact discovered and kept: the raycast is NOT a clean mirror under reversal. B->A casts [B,P,Q,A], not the reverse [B,Q,P,A], because a box nested in a wider one is entered AFTER it from BOTH ends (near-face order is not the mirror of far-face order). line_slice reverses cleanly by center-projection negation; line_raycast is direction-truthful and deeper.
obs Entry parameter proven exact: start anchor A's entry is NEGATIVE (-1/44, stroke begins inside its own box), entries strictly ascend (-1/44, 7/44, 21/44, 43/44 over dx=44), and an oblique A->D exercises the max path: max(-1/18, -1/14) = -1/18, the x face winning, asserted by exact fraction on metal.
